  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. A fully operationalized SDGs Secretariat with the relevant tool to work with.

2. SDGs roadmap operational and action plan produced annually to facilitate the implementation of key interventions.

3. Tailor-made training materials on the SDGs available and being fully utilised to training various officers on the localization and mainstreaming of SDGs</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline: SDGs National Steering Committee</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1: Enhanced Capacity of the MFED through the SDGs National Secretariat to ably Coordinate and Lead the Implementation of SDGs in Botswana
-	Recruitment of the Project Manager within the SDGs National Secretariat
- Training of Ministerial SDG Focal Points on Roles and responsibilities
- 2 National steering committee meeting held for project oversight purposed; annual workplan consideration, implementation tracking


Output 2: Enhanced capacities of sector ministries and departments at national and subnational levels to plan for the localization and mainstreaming of the SDGs in their sector plans and budgets.
-	Capacity building to facilitate the integration of SDG targets and indicators in policy and planning frameworks
-	Support Ministries by preparing a paper on SDG Planning Guidelines
-  Train core team for 6 pilot Ministries


Output 3: A comprehensive advocacy, sensitization and awareness drive undertaken across the country on the SDGs to ensure no one is left behind. 
-	Advocacy, sensitization and awareness creation workshops: training of Media and development of Award Criteria for SDGs. A Terms of Refence was development towards this exercise in consultation with Media Institute for Botswana. An Inception report was produced 

Output 4: Enhanced support provided to policy development, knowledge products, South &#x2013; south and triangular cooperation, human development and data for the development of SDGs to inform evidence based planning, monitoring, reporting on SDGs and related strategic interventions.


-	Finalise SDGs Implementation Status Report for Botswana 
-	Provide Technical Assistance for improvement of the SDGs statistical monitoring capacity for the country</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">2 meetings of the NSC were held for appreciating the workplan and the status of project implementation . The NSC also decided for Botswana to submit a voluntary national review report at the 2022 High Level political Forum for sustainable development . The training of SDG focal points was done virtually due to Coviid19 restrictions by the Government of Botswana.
- The Roll Out commenced in 4 sectors and as at December 2021 all Ministries had facilitators appointed and were at different levels with the process. 
-Finalisation and Printing of SDGs Implementation Status Report for Botswana was done and the report was disseminated in different platforms</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
